{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"64","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Presents"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"64 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given the prices of three presents. Also there are three sisters. It is known that the most valuable present is for the eldest sister. The second (by price) is for the second sister. And the less valuable present is for the youngest sister. If two (or three) presents have the same price, corresponding sisters may get the in a random way."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains three integer numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, a3"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ a1, a2, a3 ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the prices of the presents."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print three numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i1, i2, i3"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ i1, i2, i3 ≤ 3"},{"kind":"text","text":"), all of them should be distinct. The first number stands for the seniority of the sister which will get the first present (1 stands for 